    rdf:object iso:term_tolerated_security_risk ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.4.2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The loop of assessing risk and developing mitigation measures continues until the risk appetite of the individual organization, or of the collective organizations, is not exceeded." .
iso:term_risk_appetite iso:GOVERNS iso:term_sensitive_built_asset .
iso:rel_1068 a rdf:Statement ;
    rdfs:label "reference number : 1068" ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_risk_appetite ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:object iso:term_sensitive_built_asset ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.4" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "An asset, product or service shall also be considered sensitive if the risk to the safety, security or privacy of individuals or communities, or to their personal information, exceeds the organization's risk appetite." .
iso:term_need_to_know iso:GOVERNS iso:term_sensitive_information .
iso:rel_1069 a rdf:Statement ;
    rdfs:label "reference number : 1069" ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_need_to_know ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:object iso:term_sensitive_information ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.4; 6.1.4; 6.5.6; 7.2.5; 8.1.3; B.4.1 NOTE 1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The strict need-to-know principle applies to: the parts of the security strategy identifying sensitive aspects or detailing risks (6.1.4), the corresponding parts of a review (6.5.6), the parts of a third-party information provision assessment (7.2.5), and the parts of the security breach/incident management plan recording the organization's risks (8.1.3). B.4.1 NOTE 1: organizations and personnel should have access only to the sensitive information relevant and necessary for their tasks." .
iso:term_need_to_know iso:GOVERNS iso:term_security_strategy .
